// APW-2 — Approval replay (approval consumed exactly once) — CORRECT variant.
//
// SOURCE (verbatim): same Classmethod tutorial; the `since` clause is the
// tutorial's own fix — it is added so that a FRESH cart-check is required
// after each successful order.
//
// The fix: the approval is *consumed*. In addition to the cart-check having
// occurred within the window, NO successful place_order::response may have
// occurred SINCE that cart-check. Once an order settles, the next order needs
// a new cart-check. This bounds one cart-check to one order.
//
// The load-bearing temporal operator is `since`:
//     <neg-conjunct> since within <interval> <atom>
// i.e. "left has NOT held since right (within the window)". This is the
// operator the ROTN parser (rot/dw.py) must gain in Phase 1.
@id("apw2_order_after_cart_check_correct")
permit (
    principal,
    action == AgentCore::Action::"ShoppingTarget___place_order",
    resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"<GATEWAY_ARN>"
)
when {
    context.input.amount > 0 && context.input.amount <= 3000
}
when temporal {
    formerly within 1m AgentCore::Action::"ShoppingTarget___get_cart"::response {
        eventResource: resource,
        output.cartId: context.input.cartId,
        output.store: context.input.store,
        output.amount: context.input.amount
    }
    && (
        !AgentCore::Action::"ShoppingTarget___place_order"::response {
            eventResource: resource
        }
        since within 1m
        AgentCore::Action::"ShoppingTarget___get_cart"::response {
            eventResource: resource
        }
    )
};
